{"author":{"id":"29588b87a98184856c6eb9104921c34cca98a9cb029a2ee86cc10622d693ba86"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1794875246,"nonce":"bUZbjKN287UProANXlP04BdLoWM=","target":"ec7815a3c108b559888c136b045b913cacf62e45d47bd3cebf32a71b6d08cdfa","message":"While reading the keyboard handling we noticed that a key chord such as Alt+F, which a menu bar would use as a mnemonic, is not excluded from text input. If that is right, the letter would be inserted into a focused text field as well as triggering the shortcut.\n\nWhat the source shows (current main, and the commit we build on, cf925af):\n\n- The desktop key handler turns every key press with a character into a TEXT_INPUT event and skips it only when Ctrl or Meta is held; Alt is passed on (crates/blinc_app/src/windowed/event_loop/input/keyboard.rs:238-250 on main; :244-258 on cf925af, where Ctrl+Alt is additionally allowed for AltGr).\n- TextInput and TextArea ignore TEXT_INPUT only when ctx.ctrl or ctx.meta is set; ctx.alt is never read (crates/blinc_layout/src/widgets/text_input/handlers.rs:372-374, crates/blinc_layout/src/widgets/text_area/handlers.rs:249-256, same on both).\n- On main the character comes from the key itself (keyboard.rs:82), so Alt+F yields 'f' regardless of the platform. On cf925af it comes from the text winit reports (keyboard.rs:84-85, extensions/blinc_platform_desktop/src/input.rs); whether that text is empty for an Alt chord depends on the platform and we have not checked it.\n\nWe have only read the code and have not reproduced this yet, so please treat it as a possible issue. We will add a minimal reproduction here once we have one.","files":null}]}